  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e6bcb85197f7e9c40a5a71a5116a5211, type: 3}
  m_Name: Piotr Anatolievich
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PassengerData
  passengerName: Piotr Anatolievich
  portrait: {fileID: 4130640169021434097, guid: 1f8bd4a49a1ddfc4e881a6d689aa8569, type: 3}
  healthPoints: 3
  charDescription: Piotr is a man in his late thirties. Mustachioed with very short
    hair graying at the temples and bushy eyebrows, his chiseled face evokes an impassive
    man, a quiet strength. As a former factory worker, his great muscular power is
    a great advantage in the face of the dangers of the rails. Difficult to access,
    his sensitive point is family. Talking to him about it allows him to open up.
    He is actually a widower, an incendiary bomb having killed his wife. He had been
    trying for a long time to have a child, and his wife's death devastated him.
    He is now terrified of fire, freezing him on the spot. He carries with him the
    ashes of his wife, which he wishes to scatter in the free zone, where the war
    does not strike as she deserves eternal rest.
  bonus:
  - fort
  - sang froid
  - peur du feu
  inkJSON: {fileID: 0}
